00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.980
You stole the Arctic Pearl?

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.780
I thought you found it!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.890
My Zackbots found it in the Arctic Museum!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.830
It's a funny story, really.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.270
You promised me pearls, Zack. I want pearls now!

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:47.060
And we need to make like a pearl and roll!

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.950
Hey! Get that pearl!

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:49.680
Oops.

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:53.050
GET IT!

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:59.600
I am so not impressed.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.560
Quick, Martin! With walrus power, we can find the pearl before they do!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:14.240
Guys, hang on! Jimmy's sending you the whisker attachment disc!

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.270
Way to save the day, Aviva!

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:22.490
Okay, if I were a walrus, I'd use my whiskers to feel in the mud.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:25.670
Sifting through with walrus whisker power.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:29.030
Gotta find that pearl!

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.090
It's 7 o'clock, Martin!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.040
I can't understand you, Chris.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:38.130
You've got the arctic pearl in your mouth!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:42.430
Uh, Martin, you said that a little loud too!

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.450
Martin, go long!

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:49.110
Got it!

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:57.450
Swim, Martin!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.450
Hey, Zackbox! Is this what you want?

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:06.260
good walrus move, Martin!

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:09.400
Not good enough, Chris!

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:18.440
Help! Over here!

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.440
Hang on, bro. I've got an idea that might work.

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:23.190
All I need now is a clam.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.690
Haven't you eaten enough?

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.630
Ha! Found one!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:30.000
An octopus can't resist a tasty clam.

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:40.090
Oh, that's gonna cost me.

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:42.780
The herd's in trouble, Chris.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:45.980
After 13 minutes without air,

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:47.870
they're becoming really weak,

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.870
and after 20, they drown.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.870
It's been 14 minutes.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.920
But this thing's a maze of numbers and buttons.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.220
It'll take forever to dismantle it.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:58.220
It's a maze of numbers and buttons.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:19:59.920
It'll take forever to dismantle it.

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.720
We have no choice.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:05.300
Let's give Zack the pearl so the herd can breathe.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.660
Wait a second, guys.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:09.300
Zack and I spent a summer together at science camp.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.160
Maybe I can crack the code.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.800
Not so fast, little miss Smarty Pants.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.560
Zack's favorite number is 22.

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:18.520
He has six toes on his left foot,

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:20.180
eats four radish sandwiches a day,

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.920
his favorite color is chartreuse,

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:25.360
and his favorite person is himself.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:28.660
Oh, you think you're so smart, Smarty Pants?

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.000
Well, I've got a

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.100
Let's see your thingies up my sleeve.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.840
- Yeah, you did it! - Way to go, Diva!

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.680
- Breathe, Walrus Buddies, breathe.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.320
- Now we've gotta save Blobby.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.550
- Arctic Pearl coming up, Donita.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.510
Thanks to my Insta-Freeze device,

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:58.290
they're not going anywhere.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.000
Yuh!

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:11.520
a lockdown. Let's see them get out of this one. You're trapped wild rats, and I've got

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:14.850
the baby seal thingy. Gimme the pearl!

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:23.770
Oh, we've only got 20 seconds left of air! And this ice! It's eight inches thick! We

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:30.000
can't break through it! That's thick enough to hold a two-and-a-half-ton

00:21:30.000 --> 00:22:00.000
truck. The best bro I ever had. 10 seconds. 9. 8. Back at ya Chris. 4. Unbelievable. Ice smashing heads. Lucky for us a creature that finds its food under the ice has a built-in helmet that helps it bust

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.600
right back after lunch.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:03.330
Ah, big whoop!

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.500
I've still got the tubby baby!

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:07.170
Give me the pearl!

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:11.330
Uh, Zack, you really don't want to be holding Blobby right now.

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.280
He's been eating clams all day.

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:18.050
Plus, it's not a good idea to get between a wild animal mom and her baby.

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:24.330
But look at the time! I better make like a pearl and roll!

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.880
Hey, that's my line!

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:37.100
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:41.150
Aw, cute!

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:43.410
Ah, looks like Blobby and his mom

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:45.410
are going back to where they belong.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:47.940
Take care, little buddy!

00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:51.480
And the Arctic Pearl will be back where it belongs, too.

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:54.600
And everything's back to normal in the Bering Sea.

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:56.570
And mystery solved!

00:22:56.570 --> 00:22:59.630
Now we know why walruses look so weird.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.340
Blubbery bodies to keep the Mormon cold water where their food lives

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:09.690
Giant tusks the drag along the sea bottom cool whiskers to find clams in the muck

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:13.480
Big powerful lips just suck the clam into their mouths

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:18.210
And even an ice-bashing head to get back through the ice when they're done with dinner

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:24.640
Walruses look the way they do because of where they live what they eat and how they get it and

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:28.550
Jimmy looks the way he does because of what he eats and how he gets it

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:30.000
*laughter*

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:37.420
I love weird looking creatures.

00:23:37.420 --> 00:23:43.420
Walrus, moose, every creature's face is different.

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:46.580
And it's fun to figure out why they look the way they do.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:48.560
Okay, Martin, what are some of the weirdest

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.060
creature faces you can think of?

00:23:50.060 --> 00:23:50.940
- Let's see.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:53.120
Gelata baboon, with that lip flip.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:59.120
That face tells other baboons to back off.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:15.070
Nice one, and don't forget elephants, imagine having a nose like that!

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:22.720
It can strip the wood right off a tree, it can pick up leaves, scratch her itchy eye,

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:24.840
and even give herself dust baths!

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.310
Imagine having a nose that can even chase away lions.

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:45.080
Warthog, they use their tusks for fighting.

00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:47.080
And the warts help protect their faces

00:24:47.080 --> 00:24:49.040
from the other Warthog's tusks.

00:24:49.040 --> 00:24:56.750
And its face is a shovel too.

00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:57.620
Nice!

00:24:57.620 --> 00:24:59.600
Then there's the giant anteater.

00:25:02.490 --> 00:25:05.030
with a face that reaches way down low

00:25:05.030 --> 00:25:07.670
to link up termites with a super long tongue.

00:25:13.360 --> 00:25:16.160
Wildebeest, rhino, vulture, tortoise, stork.

00:25:16.590 --> 00:25:17.680
We could go on forever.

00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:19.980
All weird faces, all for a purpose.

00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:22.520
And there's nothing weird about that.

00:25:25.330 --> 00:25:28.650
And you know, maybe they think we're the weird-looking ones.

00:25:29.130 --> 00:25:30.000
With our small...

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:36.420
noses, our little lips, our furless faces, our round ears.

00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:37.420
So what do you think, girl?

00:25:37.420 --> 00:25:41.510
Are we the weird looking ones?

00:25:41.510 --> 00:25:45.170
Thought so.

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:47.990
So get out there on a creature adventure of your own.

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:51.950
And look for animals with weird looking and useful faces.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.840
Catch you on the creature trail!

